# Assets. The folder layout is committed (a .gitkeep holds each one open, since git
# does not track empty folders) so a fresh clone shows where a game's images and
# audio go: shared ones in assets/, per-target ones in assets/<target>/. The art
# and sound inside are the game's, not Matchbox's, and stay local.
assets/**
!assets/**/
!assets/**/.gitkeep

# Executables. Every tool in tools/ is built from the .odin file beside it
# (see tools/howto.md), so a committed .exe is only a stale copy of its source.
*.exe

# Debug files the Odin compiler writes next to an executable.
*.pdb
*.rdi
*.ilk

# Build output. 3ds_build.bat writes romfs/ (converted images and audio),
# odin_asm/ (the assembly it links) and the .elf / .smdh / .3dsx it packages.
# vita_build.bat uses the same build/ and odin_asm/, and packs a .vpk.
build/
romfs/
odin_asm/
*.elf
*.smdh
*.3dsx
*.vpk

# console_deploy.local.ini holds anything private (a password) that the committed
# tools/console_deploy.ini must not.
tools/console_deploy.local.ini

# Local reference material, not the repository's to share.
3ds_adv_prog_man.html
